      "order": 7,
      "text": "We use similar language to that on page 210, with appropriate modifications:"
    },
    {
      "category": "text_block",
      "order": 8,
      "text": "The SLR(1) parsing algorithm. Let s be the current state whose number is at the top of the parsing stack. Then actions are defined as follows:"
    },
    {
      "category": "text_block",
      "order": 9,
      "text": "(1) If state s contains any item of the form $ A \\to\\alpha. X \\beta $ ,where X is a terminal, and X is the next token in the input string, then the action is to remove the current input token and push onto the stack the number of the state containing the item $ A \\to\\alpha X. \\beta $"
